                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I got this from a sketchy giveaway site.\n\"Undefined\" fits very well, because I can't define what this game is supposed to be. It's kind of like a tech demo without the tech. Not worth buying.\nThe graphics are very basic, which is fine. However, what is not fine is that there's only one option - setting the resolution in a settings screen similar to Unity. In fact, there's no menu at all, so if you want to close the game, you have to tab out or press Alt+F4. Also, the game runs at a whopping (estimated) 15 fps.\nOnce you're in the game, it's straight to the \"action\". There are a few arrows leading you somewhere. I don't know where though, because when I followed them, I got outside and managed to fall out of bounds. Until I found out, that I was not supposed to go there but down instead where the arrows continue. A few jump passages await you on your way to whatever. They feel very specific about what you can stand on.\nThe controls are horrible. It's not because they're bad, it's because the camera is having a constant seizure. If you move your mouse, it just feels choppy, but walking up slopes or walking into walls makes your camera go apeshit. Combined with the framerate, it gives you motion sickness.\nThe sound is nonexistant except for a loud introduction of white noise before going full silent.\nI can't recommend this game at this point. There's nothing to see here. I'm genuinely impressed that I even got so much to write about this game.",
